<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22322" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλίχομαι</span></b> , only pres. and
		impf., exc. aor. 1
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγλιξάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					241
				</span></i>
			:—<i>cling to, strive after, long for</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.72
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἰγύπτου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.152
				</span></i>
			 (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. περὶ ἐλευθερίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.102
				</span></i>
			 (s. v. l.)); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῦτ᾽ ἦν ὦν μάλιστ᾽ ἐγλίχετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					5.22
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. τοῦ ζῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					117a
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Charond.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.2.24
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κράτους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Char.</u>
					26.1
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				17
			</span></i> (dub.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Hipparch.</u>
			</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				226e
			</span></i>: folld. by a relat. clause, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλιχόμεθα τὴν μᾶζαν ἵνα λευκὴ παρῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					141.7
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς στρατηγήσεις γλίχεαι</span>
			how thou shalt become general, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.161
			</span></i>: c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὧν ἐγλίχοντο μὴ ἅψασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					8.15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰδέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					489d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					6.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποστερῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					18.207
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					86.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θιγεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>D.</u>
					3.1
				</span></i>
			.—Not in 
				Ep.
			 or Trag. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλῐ-</span>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλίχων [ῑ</span>] is 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλήχων</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
			</span></i> Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.37
			</span></i>.)</div>
